  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759795,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Music Construction Set for Commodore 64: Compose Your Own Soundtrack!\n\nStep back in time and unleash your inner composer with Music Construction Set for the Commodore 64! This groundbreaking 1983 program, originally designed for the Apple II, revolutionized music creation with its intuitive graphical user interface – a truly novel concept for the era. Forget complex notation; simply drag and drop notes onto the musical staff to build your own melodies and harmonies. Play back your creations through the C64’s built-in sound hardware, and even print your compositions.\n\nWhile joystick control is required for note-by-note creation, the payoff is immense: the ability to craft original music without needing formal training. The program even includes sample songs to inspire your own creations.  For an enhanced experience, consider connecting external hardware for richer sound.  Music Construction Set for the C64 is a powerful and enjoyable tool, suitable for both budding songwriters and seasoned musicians alike, proving to be a joy to use and a testament to the creative possibilities of early home computing."
    },
